1
00:00:03,401 --> 00:00:16,657
Now B2, the 3-drawer base. Click its pencil.

2
00:00:16,657 --> 00:00:24,689
Match the sink base: 34-1/2" high and 23-1/4" deep.

3
00:00:24,689 --> 00:00:29,920
Drawers: how many, and the slide. The drawer boxes are built to suit.

4
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:34,432
Slides are Blum TANDEM, 15, 18 or 21 in. Auto picks the length from the cabinet depth.

5
00:00:34,432 --> 00:00:48,525
Explode the model to see the drawer boxes and the slide holes bored in the sides.

6
00:00:48,525 --> 00:00:56,333
The editor flags things to check, like drawer sides thicker than TANDEM allows.

7
00:00:56,333 --> 00:01:16,849
Next, B3, the 2-door base: 30" wide, same height and depth.

8
00:01:16,849 --> 00:01:22,643
Doors and hinges: none, one or a pair, the gap, and the hinge cup boring.

9
00:01:22,643 --> 00:01:27,037
Hinges are Salice Silentia+ 110°: 35 mm cups with 3 mm plates, bored automatically.

10
00:01:27,037 --> 00:01:33,227
The black dots in 3D are the hinge cups, plates and shelf-pin holes.

11
00:01:33,227 --> 00:01:40,663
Edgebanding: click any edge of any part in the list to change its band.

12
00:01:40,663 --> 00:01:51,372
Add hole puts an extra hole on any part, typed in by position, size and depth.

13
00:01:51,372 --> 00:02:11,580
Last base, B4: one door, 15" wide.

14
00:02:11,580 --> 00:02:23,511
With one door you choose the hinge side. Make this one hinge on the right.
